THOUGHT: My previous sed edit mangled the code (duplicate variable, missing inlInsn). I need to fix InlineMethods.inlineMethod by introducing a non-null local inlInsn using Objects.requireNonNull, then using it for copyWithoutResult() and isAssignNeeded(...). I’ll carefully patch the method body with sed, then re-run the Gradle compile to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '80,88c\	private void inlineMethod(MethodNode mth, MethodNode callMth, MethodInlineAttr mia, BlockNode block, InvokeNode insn) {
		InsnNode inlInsn = java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(
				mia.getInsn(),
				"MethodInlineAttr insn must be non-null when notNeeded() is false");
		InsnNode inlCopy = inlInsn.copyWithoutResult();
		RegisterArg resultArg = insn.getResult();
		if (resultArg != null) {
			inlCopy.setResult(resultArg.duplicate());
		} else if (isAssignNeeded(inlInsn, insn, callMth)) {
			// add fake result to make correct java expression (see test TestGetterInlineNegative)
			inlCopy.setResult(makeFakeArg(mth, callMth.getReturnType(), "unused"));
		}' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/visitors/InlineMethods.java && nl -ba jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/dex/visitors/InlineMethods.java | sed -n '76,100p' && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && tail -n 60 new_build_output.log
```

